  (text "GATE_KILL reaches the two high sides through the driver's own SHUTDOWN input, not through a clamp -- a ground-referenced kill FET cannot short a gate\nthat floats 100 V up. Nothing is drawn for it here because the driver is not chosen; see the note at the foot of the sheet." (at 150.0 128.0 0)
